            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0319" n="309" xml:id="pg309"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.43 Institute of Pacific Relations/197:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Atcheson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-07T23:00:00-04:00">August 7, 1943—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1053. Department has been notified by Institute of Pacific Relations that Edward
                    C. Carter and W. L. Holland, representatives of that organization, are now en
                    route to China.</p>
                <p>We understand that Dr. T. V. Soong has already notified the interested Chinese
                    officials in Chungking of Mr. Carter’s approaching visit.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
